PN,31604
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F316A1785633476
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FThis will be the second dead rocket
OL,7,Fknown to crash into the moon
OL,8,Faccidentally. A Chinese rocket segment
OL,9,Fdug out a pair of craters on the lunar
OL,10,Ffar side in 2022.
OL,12,FWednesday's crash will cause a flash
OL,13,Flasting less than a second and will
OL,14,Flikely be too dim to see, experts say.
OL,16,FHowever, stargazers will be excited to
OL,17,Fknow the stream of ejected material
OL,18,Fcould stretch for several miles into
OL,19,Fspace and remain visible through
OL,20,Ftelescopes for tens of minutes.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
