PN,31605
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F316A1785633476
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FBenjamin Fernando, a scientist from
OL,7,FLos Alamos National Laboratory, said
OL,8,Fthe moon's low gravity and lack of
OL,9,Fwind will prevent the dust from
OL,10,Fblowing away.
OL,12,F"Part of the reason for our interest
OL,13,Fin this event is to figure out how
OL,14,Fmuch of a hazard debris impacts pose
OL,15,Fto future astronauts," he added in an
OL,16,Femail.
OL,18,FFernando anticipates an impact crater
OL,19,Fnearly 27 metres across and five
OL,20,Fmetres deep, too small to see from
OL,21,FEarth but visible to spacecraft.
OL,26,@tD@AOUwD@VO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/9
