PN,31606
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F316A1785633476
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FBefore and after shots of the event
OL,7,Fwill be captured by NASA's Lunar
OL,8,FReconnaissance Orbiter and South
OL,9,FKorea's Danuri lunar orbiter.
OL,11,FThe Danuri orbiter is expected to
OL,12,Fstray within a mile or two of the
OL,13,Frocket just two minutes before it
OL,14,Fcrashes into the moon.
OL,16,FThe abandoned SpaceX rocket segment,
OL,17,Fmeasuring 12 meters and weighing
OL,18,Faround 4,500 kilograms hoisted two
OL,19,Fprivate lunar landers in January last
OL,20,Fyear.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
