PN,31608
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F316A1785633476
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FDecades later, in 2009, NASA
OL,7,Fintentionally crashed its LCROSS
OL,8,Fspacecraft and upper stage in search
OL,9,Fof ice near the lunar south pole.
OL,11,FWith the moon as the new travel hot
OL,12,Fspot, scientists said it's crucial to
OL,13,Fimprove debris monitoring and traffic
OL,14,Fcontrol before packs of robots and
OL,15,Fastronauts arrive.
OL,17,FThe United States and China are racing
OL,18,Fto land astronauts on the moon in the
OL,19,Fnext few years.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
